{:edb/db-before-t 2113 :edb/db-after-t 2114 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535426 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:50:17.829Z" 13194139535426 true] [17592186083292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348621 13194139535426 true] [17592186083292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348642 13194139535426 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348618 13194139535426 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348628 13194139535426 true] [17592186083293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348635 13194139535426 true] [17592186348618 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348619 13194139535426 true] [17592186348618 1089 "q-276486" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348618 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535426 true] [17592186348618 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $320$ and the common ratio is $4?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348618 1113 #uuid "a5731125-307e-51c6-9f9a-f16cf62d6761" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348618 1145 "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 320 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 320 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}({4}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348620 13194139535426 true] [17592186348619 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535426 true] [17592186348619 1041 "field-1" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348619 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348620 13194139535426 true] [17592186348619 1110 #uuid "6171aebd-b144-5756-9dde-eb8785171ba3" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348620 1034 "\\frac{5}{3}(4^N-1)" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348620 1111 #uuid "fbb9e2ef-e6f4-5842-a54f-22a5a581cf07" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348622 13194139535426 true] [17592186348621 1089 "q-39996" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535426 true] [17592186348621 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $3+15+75+⋯\\,?$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348621 1113 #uuid "968d763f-7575-5b03-8e25-e8e3c2bafb23" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348621 1145 "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=5.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{1-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348623 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348624 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348625 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348626 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348627 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1041 "selection" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348623 13194139535426 true] [17592186348622 1110 #uuid "bd5b44dc-ca0f-5f74-81cc-6b5116cc8922" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348623 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}({5