n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{3(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & ={4}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348630 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348631 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348632 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348633 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348634 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1041 "selection" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348630 13194139535426 true] [17592186348629 1110 #uuid "9124a7fe-87cf-5f88-be2b-e8c915c23b03" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348630 1034 "{4}^{N}-1" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348630 1111 #uuid "c856e8d0-7aa7-5451-8e1d-432d7978f28a" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348631 1034 "{4}^{N}-12" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348631 1111 #uuid "1ee4b3bb-2e41-5c34-8d7a-5d57d77bf837" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348632 1034 "4({3}^{N}-1)" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348632 1111 #uuid "3955e9ec-c0be-5304-aa2f-c1504cba7382" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348633 1034 "3({4}^{N}-1)" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348633 1111 #uuid "a87447b3-4978-57b6-88e3-a3b4fc692a91" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348634 1034 "{3}^{N}-1" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348634 1111 #uuid "fd9fe08c-7ac4-5c96-8a4a-2c0643379b7e" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348635 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348636 13194139535426 true] [17592186348635 1089 "q-73425" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348635 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535426 true] [17592186348635 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $384$ and the common ratio is $4?$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348635 1113 #uuid "9360a987-6868-5ee3-a005-1b57385aa970" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348635 1145 "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{3} \\\\ 384 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-2(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =2({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348637 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348638 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348639 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348640 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348641 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1041 "selection" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348637 13194139535426 true] [17592186348636 1110 #uuid "92b18c56-2e57-5839-acc8-ce5670f616a7" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348637 1034 "2({4}^{N}-1)" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348637 1111 #uuid "2389d4a2-b843-5528-9175-9f2fd09ff939" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348638 1034 "{4}^{N}-1" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348638 1111 #uuid "ea7adb18-dbfe-5840-975c-125e7a68beeb" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348639 1034 "{4}^{N}-2" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348639 1111 #uuid "25f2836d-01f8-5701-bb63-b68b0ebfdda2" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348640 1034 "3({4}^{N}-1)" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348640 1111 #uuid "2c5301bb-0b79-5e78-8fd1-fddf6a2df8db" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348641 1034 "{4}^{N}-3" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535426 true] [17592186348641 1111 #uuid "b999a01c-f4e0-5c76-83d4-2036f54dc55b" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348642 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348643 13194139535426 true] [17592186348642 1089 "q-9749" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348642 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535426 true] [17592186348642 1100 "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a series $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯?$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348642 1113 #uuid "78fba3be-7310-5e50-9e3c-f6710527699a" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348642 1145 "Note that $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯$ is the sum of a geometric series since the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nFirst, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{3}\\cdot ({4}^{N}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535426 true] [17592186348643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348644 13194139535426 true] [17592186348643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348645 131941395